    "summary": "Rare acoustic gems, strong Cosmic Charlie, but mix hiccups.",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a rare acoustic set highlighted by How Long Blues and deep‑elm jams, then erupts into electric fireworks with a monster Cosmic Charlie. China>Rider and The Other One provide high‑energy peaks, though mix issues and missing cuts mar the flow.",
    "review": "July 14, 1970 at the Euphoria Ballroom captures one of those oddball Dead nights where acoustic tradition meets psychedelic surge. After opening with folk‑rock staples like Don't Ease Me In and Dire Wolf, the band slipped into a seldom‑heard acoustic segment featuring a plaintive How Long Blues and a rolling Deep Elem Blues that showcase Garcia’s warm, classic tone. The second half flips the switch – New Speedway Boogie launches a high‑octane electric set where China>Rider and a thunderous The Other One roar through the room, only to be undercut by mix problems that dull the clarity of tracks like Casey Jones and the buzzing on the later numbers. Cosmic Charlie stands out as a monster jam, and despite missing portions of Easy Wind and Good Lovin', the energy stays high. The night closes with an inspired Uncle John's Band encore, leaving fans with a memorable blend of rarity and raw power.",
